  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Revitalized livelihood of agribusinesses in the livestock sector for improved food security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Revitalized livelihood of agribusinesses in the livestock sector for improved food security project aims to enhance food security and socio-economic revitalization of meat and dairy producers in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Punjab. The project focuses on improving productivity, compliance, and competitiveness of the meat and dairy sectors by leveraging international expertise, particularly from Italy, and fostering innovation among rural communities and small and medium enterprises (SMEs). Key objectives include strengthening regulatory frameworks, establishing training and capacity-building initiatives, and promoting sustainable business practices. The project will support knowledge transfer, enhance food safety standards, and improve market access, ultimately creating a robust and resilient livestock sector that contributes to improved livelihoods and food security in Pakistan. The project is supported by the Italian Agency for Development Cooperation (AICS), which plays a pivotal role in facilitating intern ational collaboration and funding. AICS, through its financing, aims to foster economic growth and sustainable development in Pakistan by leveraging Italian expertise and technology to strengthen the dairy and meat sectors. In addition, the involvement of UNIDO#s ITPO Italy, will enable the transfer of adva</narrative>
  </description>
